TITLE:: BNUnitTest
SUMMARY:: Project UnitTest subclass with helpers and a runner for all of its test suites.
CATEGORIES:: Testing
RELATED:: Classes/UnitTest

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::BNUnitTest:: is the base class for this project's unit tests. It adds assertion and ordinal helpers used by several suites. LINK::#*runAll:: sets CODE::UnitTest.reportPasses_(false):: and runs every direct or nested subclass of TELETYPE::BNUnitTest::. LINK::Classes/UnitTest#*runAll:: cannot be used for this: it only runs when called on LINK::Classes/UnitTest:: itself.

Suites that subclass LINK::Classes/UnitTest:: directly (for example CODE::PlayableNoteUnitTests:: and CODE::ArrayedCollectionUnitTests::) are not included.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: runAll
Sets CODE::UnitTest.reportPasses_(false)::, resets pass/fail state, runs each TELETYPE::BNUnitTest:: subclass sequentially, then prints the combined report. Leaves pass reporting off afterwards.

RETURNS::
The routine started by CODE::forkIfNeeded::, or the result of the last expression if already inside a routine.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: assertWithMessage
Records a pass or fail from a boolean condition. On failure, CODE::failureMessage:: is reported; on pass, the recorded message is empty. Returns the condition so callers can stop further checks after a failure.

ARGUMENT:: condition
A LINK::Classes/Boolean::; true records a pass, false a fail.

ARGUMENT:: failureMessage
The message posted when the condition is false.

ARGUMENT:: details
Optional extra failure detail passed through to LINK::Classes/UnitTest#-failed::.

RETURNS::
CODE::true:: or CODE::false::, matching CODE::condition::.

METHOD:: getOrdinal
Formats an integer as an English ordinal string (CODE::1st::, CODE::2nd::, CODE::3rd::, CODE::4th::, and so on), including the CODE::12th:: / CODE::13th:: special cases.

ARGUMENT:: number
An LINK::Classes/Integer:: index or count.

ARGUMENT:: assumeZeroBased
When CODE::true:: (the default), CODE::number:: is treated as a zero-based index and incremented before formatting, so CODE::0:: becomes CODE::1st::. When CODE::false::, CODE::number:: is formatted as given.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/String::.

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
(
BNUnitTest.runAll;
)
::
